            <ArticleTitle>Papilledema without peripheral neuropathy in a patient taking perhexiline maleate.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>173-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Perhexiline maleate is an agent currently under investigation in Canada that is used for angina unresponsive to other treatment. This paper describes a possible side effect previously unreported--papilledema not associated with peripheral neuropathy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
